            <ArticleTitle>Neuromodulators for the treatment of headache disorders and fibromyalgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>333-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Migraine and fibromyalgia are prevalent and disabling disorders with few preventive medications approved by the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA). Neuromodulators (or antiepileptic drugs; AEDs) are often effective in the treatment of these conditions. Divalproex sodium and topiramate are FDA-approved AEDs for migraine. For fibromyalgia, pregabalin has recently been approved in the United States. We review the use of AEDs in the preventive treatment of these highly prevalent disorders.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
